# Import MODULES any FSRING driver image may reference.
# One module name per line, case-insensitive; '#' starts a comment.
# Growth is deliberate: a slice that needs a new module adds it here in the
# same commit, so review sees it. Slice C3 measured all three release images at
# 44 symbol pairs across exactly these two modules. Wdmsec.lib contributes
# static code and downstream ntoskrnl.exe imports; there is no wdmsec.sys
# runtime import.
ntoskrnl.exe

# ksecdd.sys - BCryptGenRandom, the ONLY randomness source
# 11-rust-implementation.md section 4 permits ("Time, counters, PIDs,
# RtlRandom*, and daemon-supplied bytes are never entropy... There is no weaker
# fallback"). The compliant source is not in the WDM base header set, so
# fsring-sys hand-declares it and links km/x64/ksecdd.lib.
#
# Added by slice A3. This is the FIRST module beyond ntoskrnl.exe, and the
# widening is deliberate: the alternative is a forbidden entropy source.
ksecdd.sys
